[Task Description]
Define rules that torch.polygamma API parameters should satisfy. Refer to the API documentation. Particularly, there should be at least one rule to suppress each error message.

Type is encoded as an integer (index of the following list):
[bool, np.int8, np.int16, np.int32, np.int64, np.uint8, np.float16, np.float32, np.float64, np.complex64, np.complex128, str, np.dtype]

String value should be selected from the following list:
["ii", "ii->i", "i,j->ij", "bij,bjk->bik", "...ij->...ji", "bn,anm,bm->ba", "none", "mean", "sum", "max", "min", "relu", "tanh", "sigmoid", "softmax", "elu", "selu", "gelu", "swish", "softplus", "linear", "constant", "reflect", "replicate", "circular", "nearest", "bilinear", "bicubic", "trilinear", "area", "linear"]

[API Documentation]
polygamma(n, input, *, out=None) -> Tensor

Alias for :func:`torch.special.polygamma`.

[API Signature] n: integer, input: tensor, out: tensor

[Error Messages]
TypeError: polygamma(): argument 'out' must be Tensor, not float
RuntimeError: polygamma(n, x) does not support negative n.
RuntimeError: "polygamma" not implemented for 'ComplexDouble'
RuntimeError: result type ComplexDouble can't be cast to the desired output type Bool

